# Cold start (Cursor)

**At session start, before other work:**

```bash
.venv/bin/python scripts/cursor_cold_start.py
```

The script fetches `/api/rules`. Cursor already has `AGENTS.md` + `CLAUDE.md` as workspace rules; those are digests, not a substitute for `/api/rules`.

## Do not fetch at boot

- `/api/session/current?agent=orchestrator` — wrong agent lane
- `context_canary.py mint` — 1M orchestrator only
- `Read` on `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`

## Fetch at boot

| Need | Call |
| --- | --- |
| Rules hash and sources | `/api/rules?format=json` (the script) |

## Fetch on demand

| Need | Call |
| --- | --- |
| Rules for a task or phase | `/api/rules?scope=task:<name>` (selector: `agents_extensions/shared/rules/task-scoped-reading.md`) |
| Full ruleset | `/api/rules?format=markdown` — full policy audits, ambiguous cross-cutting tasks |
| Fleet inbox | `/api/comms/inbox?agent=cursor` |
| Dispatches | `/api/delegate/active` |
| Track state | `/api/state/summary` |
| One module | `/api/state/module/{track}/slug/{slug}` |
| After commit | `/api/orient?fresh=true` |

Protocol: `agents_extensions/cursor/rules/cold-start.md`
